WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.900
Hi! It's my birthday! HURRAY!

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.420
It's, uh, it's actually tomorrow. HURRAY!

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.840
I'm turning 27! HURRAY!

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.760
Someone told me I'm almost 30... HURRAY!

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:13.180
And I'm dying... Hurruhh...

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.140
It's actually very weird to think that when I
started this whole Youtube thing,

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.540
I was actually 22 years old.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.040
And NOW look at me!

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.600
What the hell happened?!

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.120
Either way I'm old, it doesn't matter.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.720
But I just got back from VidCon

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.400
and it was an amazing time.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.520
I-I got to meet so many other Youtubers

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.620
and some of them mm-my favorite Youtubers that I haven't gotten to meet in the past like Boogie.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:35.660
I've been watching Boogie2988, uh if you didn't know

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:39.420
for a long, long time and he's big source of inspiration.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:43.440
And we got in, like, this... this circular 
ass-kissing contest to be like,

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.000
"No, YOU inspire me."

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.180
And then he was like, "No, YOU inspire ME."

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.100
And I'm like, "No, fuck you! You inspire me, asshole!"

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.820
And he's like, "YOU DICKBAG! You inspire ME!"

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:53.560
So, it's just.....

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:54.760
a bunch of that bullshit.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.240
If you haven't checked out his channel,
I'll put a link in the description below

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:01.880
He is a COOL, cool guy. You should definitely check his videos if you haven't in the past.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:05.220
And then, of course, you know, I got to hang out with the Youtubers that I've known for a long time.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.020
Uhh, Jack was there.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.240
Y'know, Ryan and Matt were there.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.780
A whole bunch of other Youtubers that I met in the past were there and the problem is...

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.760
Like with most conventions that
I go to, I get so caught up in...

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.480
being there and doing the things while I'm there,

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:25.020
that I totally forget to actually take pictures and record video because I'm a douchebag,

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.760
and I forget to actually post stuff OUT for you guys!

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.380
So in all honesty,

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:32.340
I know yo- a lot of you guys wanted
to see a collab with me and Jack

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:33.800
I forgot to do that!

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.760
Tha-there wasn't enough time!

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.380
I was busy...

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:40.140
So, I'll just have to invite him out to L.A.
again, sometime in the future,

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.040
along with, uh,

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.200
Wade and Bob.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.940
Bob NEEDS to come to L.A. PLEASE!

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.080
Tweet at Bob!

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:47.700
Tell him to come to L.A.!

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.400
He's done with schooool!

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.560
I need him!!

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:51.720
I miss him...

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:52.900
Poor Bob...

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:53.620
And Wade too.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:55.420
I guess Wade can come along too.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:57.460
But I miss those guys, they weren't at VidCon.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:59.520
And actually at VidCon, I had a panel there,

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.160
and they wanted to stick me in the giant room.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.980
They had this room with like, uhm...

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:06.220
seating for 4500 poeple.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:10.200
It's the biggest room in the place and they 
TOLD me that I would easily fill up the place,

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.560
and that was intimidating to me because
I was doing the panel by myself.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.780
Which I've never done a panel just by myself,

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:22.080
and they had an alternative, with... which was a much smaller room- it was about a 500 person room.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.960
And... it was a more intimate environment.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.200
I mean, even 500 people, still a lot of people but,

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:30.960
something smaller scale like that appeals to me more,

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:36.180
because I'm able to actually interact with people and I'm able to actually talk with people and it's not like you're

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:39.320
watching me on these weird, big projectors.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.320
I mean! Next year, I'll do it,

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:45.040
because I heard that a lot of people were very disappointed that they didn't get into the panel,

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.540
and it's something that I have to acknowledge.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:51.620
The fact that there ARE so many people out there that want to see me. And when I go to these conventions,

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:56.360
it is intimidating... to see how many people wanna meet me.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.280
And security was a big concern this year,

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:01.640
and it went very well. There was no incidents as far as I know.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.840
There may have been small incidents here and there, but

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:06.700
uh, it went relatively smoothly, uh, from my end.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.660
There was actually this one moment where, uh,

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:13.440
myself, Jack, Emma Blackery, and... Comicstorian were doing an event on the Maker Stage...

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.580
And it was really fun, it went totally well, uh,

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:20.520
some of you saw it livestreamed and we were playing Funemployed. But AFTER it was over,

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:24.740
It was the only time... that we were a little scared.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:26.360
Because... a-as you know, like,

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.660
there's a lot of people at VidCon.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:32.020
There's just so many people densely
packed on the VidCon floor,

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.800
and there were so many crowding the broo- the booth

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.700
that as soon as we got done...

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:41.180
We literally had nowhere to go. We were
trying to get backstage but it's like,

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:44.460
we stepped INTO the zombie hoard.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:48.060
Not comparing you guys to zombies or- oh, I'm an asshole now...

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.780
But not comparing you guys to zombies, but it's just like

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:55.880
so many people wanted selfies, that we were just getting phones shoved in our faces and we're getting

00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:02.200
jostled around. And I mean, i-it's flattering in a way that so many people want to meet us, but it's scary

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:07.460
when there's... a hundred people at ONCE, trying very desperately to get a picture so...

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:11.200
we were just trying to get backstage so we could go to another event because at VidCon, like

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:15.540
all of us creators are booked VERY tightly, we're going from one event to another to another to another,

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:18.820
and then we get like, an hour break for a meal then another and another and another...

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.340
And, uh, it was just...

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:23.360
Very intimidating because security was SO beefed up.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:30.040
We had like 4 burly security guard and even they were like, "HOOLY SHIT, THESE KIDS! GODDAMMIT!!!"

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.020
Apparently Santa Claus was our bodyguard this year.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:35.200
But it was jus- it was the only
moment where it's ever been intimidating.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:38.400
And I think that's just because it's VidCon. And VidCon...

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.500
Y'know, you guys who go there are MUCH more intense.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:44.140
It's like the fan-central thing.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:46.640
So, of course there's so many super fans there,

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.400
whereas if you go to PAX, y'know...

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:49.600
It's gamers,

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:50.320
it's chill,

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.340
it's whatever, y'know.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:55.200
We'r- they're mostly there for the video games and not mostly there for us.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:58.820
But VidCon is just like... ONLY the people that are there

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:01.120
so, i-it gets a little intense sometimes.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.140
But the other thing that happened at VidCon was,

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:08.740
there were 3 separate families AT VidCon that wanted to meet me from the Make-a-Wish Foundation.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:10.940
And that's a HUGE honor, like,

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:15.120
uhh, people at PAX came to meet me, uh,
from the Make-a Wish-Foundation,

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:21.060
I've done Make-a-Wish stuff before, it's a complete honor to be able to walk in that room and meet people

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:24.000
who've gone through so much struggle. And, uh,

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.740
I-It wa- It was really, like...

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:29.800
both a heartwarming and a heartbreaking experience to be able to talk to these families

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.040
And I got... I got about, like

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:34.180
we were booked so tight, like I said, that I got about half hour each

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:36.980
uh, with each of these families, just to be able to sit down and talk.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.620
And it was a great time because...

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:41.360
I walked into the first family... uh, and...

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.420
I-It was... It was like, there were very tearful
and they were so excited to see me.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:47.500
And I was just like, "Hey! How's it going?"

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:50.480
"Oh, gosh! Don't cry, I'm normal! I swear!"

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:52.480
"I-I'm weird but I'm normal."

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:54.840
An-and by the end of the conversation, y'know...

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:58.220
I-I hope they realize that I'm just a normal guy.

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:03.780
Uhh, I hope they realize that I-I relate very closely with these experiences that they have gone through,

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:04.900
and that, y'know,

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:06.860
really, really, I do care,

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:09.400
uh, about their well-being and I care about them,

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:13.700
and I care that they watch my videos to get them through these...

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:17.500
tough surgeries, y'know, chemotherapy that 
some of them have to go through

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:22.380
These harsh experiences that children should
not have to deal with but they do...

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:25.120
I'm glad that my videos can help out in any way.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:26.240
So, it was a huge honor,

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:30.740
and actually, I recorded a few videos with each of them so here they are, in all their glory.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:36.160
Hey guys, I'm here with the Make-a-Wish
Foundation, with Katie and her family, the Clemens family.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:40.160
